1
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:44,140
Thank you.

2
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,697
Crazy Crazy Rainbow Star
Will you come here with me?

3
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:09,617
Let's go to a dream of a dream?

4
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:11,720
Darling, darling!

5
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:34,980
Hey, guys, look, it's today's newspaper.

6
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:38,380
They have a big report on Annie's lobby.

7
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,482
Come on, don't leave us hanging.

8
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,660
Quick, tell us what it says.

9
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:45,700
That article is going
to decide all our fates.

10
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:46,980
Well, about that.

11
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,300
Yeah, go on.

12
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:50,317
There's nothing much to say, really.

13
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:52,280
It doesn't mention us at all.

14
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:55,560
Wait, it doesn't mention us? Really?

15
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:57,660
Not a single word?

16
00:01:58,320 --> 00:01:59,150
Nope.

17
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:00,360
We're saved!

18
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:04,955
I thought I was going to have to live
the rest of my life as a fugitive!

19
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,260
I don't get it.

20
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:10,205
The Franky family really
wrecked up the place.

21
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:11,440
Maybe your grandpa?

22
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:13,617
Like he pulled some strings and told the

23
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:16,700
government that they were
just innocent bystanders?

24
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,300
Nah, that's too complicated for him.

25
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,220
Yeah, what Luffy said!

26
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:27,277
Must be how Kiji's doing.

27
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,780
What a strange man.

28
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:31,080
At any rate, that's good for them.

29
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:33,157
Obviously, we're criminals.

30
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,457
But I would hate to see
anyone get wrapped up

31
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:37,637
in this mess and have
their whole lives ruined.

32
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:41,257
Well, good thing you feel that way,
because they had plenty to say about us.

33
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:44,040
A declaration of war on
the world government.

34
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:46,737
They even blame us for
burning down the island.

35
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:51,114
I guarantee our bounties are going to
go through the roof after this one.

36
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:55,000
Oh my gosh, does that mean I'll
finally get a bounty? Maybe.

37
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:56,905
You'll probably get something.

38
00:02:57,360 --> 00:03:00,007
But mine's going to be
the big one this time.

39
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:04,240
A bright star appears, right?

40
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:06,820
What are you excited about?

41
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,520
This is terrible news!

42
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:18,410
Hey, bro.

43
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:20,317
Iceberg's here to see you.

44
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,400
Right over there.

45
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,480
So you're really doing it.

46
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:24,720
So what?

47
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:26,488
You want to fight about it?

48
00:03:26,820 --> 00:03:28,080
Well, no.

49
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:30,960
But if you'd like, I could help you out.

50
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:34,800
Yeah, right.

51
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:37,897
You're probably just here
to mess with my head.

52
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:41,757
You've been dismantling so long,
I'm afraid your skills have dulled.

53
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,280
Show me your blueprints.

54
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:46,000
A reunion for Tom's workers, huh?

55
00:03:46,740 --> 00:03:49,916
I hope you old pros have
room for a couple of rookies.

56
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:51,690
Gah!

57
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:53,760
Galley Law Company is ready to go! No!

58
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,997
Let's build the Straw Hats a ship!

59
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,757
They're probably itching
to get off this island,

60
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,817
so we figured you could use a little help.

61
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:02,740
Well, I thought you
were repairing the city.

62
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:07,437
We were, but when we heard you were
building a new ship for the Straw Hats,

63
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,977
everyone packed up their stuff.

64
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:11,119
and ran here as fast as they could.

65
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:14,580
You guys, of course I'm happy to have you!

66
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:16,606
They really touched my heart.

67
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,030
Mine too.

68
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:21,080
Now hop to it, no slack at all!

69
00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:26,210
Yeah!

70
00:04:26,293 --> 00:04:29,074
Let's show him what the Dock
one for him and I made him!

71
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:29,990
Yeah!

72
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:38,397
Frankie's building us a ship and
we don't even have to pay for it?

73
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:39,310
All right.

74
00:04:39,393 --> 00:04:40,957
You were asleep when he said that.

75
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:41,870
Awesome!

76
00:04:41,953 --> 00:04:43,837
I guess Frankie's not a jerk after all!

77
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,117
Frankie's a nice guy!

78
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:47,317
I can't wait to see how it turns out!

79
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:48,230
Good!

80
00:04:48,313 --> 00:04:51,780
Now we can use the rest of our money
to buy supplies for the voyage.

81
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:56,457
Hope this one's equipped
with a weight room.

82
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:58,716
As long as it has cannons, I'm happy.

83
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:00,076
I think it's better.

84
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:15,100
What happened to our 100
million berries? Oh, that?

85
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,553
I already spent it all.

86
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:19,816
We needed to buy lots of
meat and booze for the party.

87
00:05:20,740 --> 00:05:21,570
Spent it?

88
00:05:21,653 --> 00:05:23,697
You spent all of my money?!

89
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:25,721
Well, everyone was really hungry.

90
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:30,477
How could you spend so much on food?

91
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:31,857
There's hardly anything left!

92
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:32,937
Of course there isn't.

93
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:34,577
The whole town was partying with us,

94
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:37,057
and they didn't go home
until morning, remember?

95
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:38,460
Sure was fun, huh?

96
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:43,977
Since the ship's free, we'll be fine.

97
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:45,700
So no worries, right?

98
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,860
I just wanted nice
furniture for this ship.

99
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:49,817
Is that so wrong?

100
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:52,460
We can still check out the resale shops.

101
00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:56,660
Hey, can I have some of
that money to go play with?

102
00:05:56,820 --> 00:05:58,980
I'd sooner take it to the grave!

103
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:01,640
Your allowance is revoked!

104
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:03,420
Yes, ma 'am!

105
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,676
Thanks for giving me this
delicious water water candy.

106
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:19,650
It's awesome.

107
00:06:19,733 --> 00:06:20,563
No problem.

108
00:06:20,646 --> 00:06:21,700
I have the money.

109
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:22,880
Why not share it?

110
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,537
With what's left over, I
want to buy a medical book.

111
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:26,460
Sounds good.

112
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:28,440
You gotta be kidding!

113
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:31,897
There's no way I'd repair your
sword for that pathetic amount!

114
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:32,862
So that's a no.

115
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,957
Come up with some more money or forget it!

116
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,000
Cranky old man.

117
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:37,950
Excuse me.

118
00:06:38,033 --> 00:06:39,717
A couple of water, water candies, please.

119
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,760
You got it. I must say.

120
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:47,017
That BBQ yesterday, it was the
best I've had in ages. Thanks.

121
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:50,218
I'd expect no less that you
use the best ingredients.

122
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:53,040
Yep, the best will do. See ya.

123
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:55,020
Goodbye, Grocery Guy!

124
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:56,042
Let's go again!

125
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:01,637
We're gonna head on back
and meet up with Granny.

126
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:02,980
See you later! Yeah!

127
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:06,100
Okay. Good night. Be careful.

128
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:09,570
Huh?

129
00:07:09,653 --> 00:07:10,900
Is that Usopp?

130
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,940
What's that? Really?

131
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:16,497
You want me to rejoin your crew, do you?

132
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:18,100
Well, I understand.

133
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:19,577
It must be rough without me.

134
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:22,937
If I'm not around, things really
start to fall apart, don't they?

135
00:07:23,020 --> 00:07:26,608
Okay, then, if you insist, I'll
rejoin the Straw Hat Pirates.

136
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:30,117
Yeah, that does seem to be
the best way to go about it.

137
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:32,080
And that makes 23 scenarios.

138
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:33,640
Hey, Chopper!

139
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:35,317
Nice weather we're having, huh?

140
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:36,400
Let's go fishing!

141
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:39,700
Hey, Luffy, care to join us?

142
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:41,060
Yeah, not bad.

143
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,937
And there's always the
just pretend like nothing

144
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:45,177
happened and hop on
board the ship strategy.

145
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:46,090
What else?

146
00:07:46,173 --> 00:07:49,037
I've decided to set out on
my own and visit Elbath.

147
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:50,237
No, please don't go!

148
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:51,496
We need you to stay!

149
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:52,517
I was just kidding!

150
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:54,917
I totally understand not wanting
to live your lives without me!

151
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,460
So, does that mean you're staying, Usopp?

152
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:00,589
Of course I will, dummies!

153
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:05,753
Man, I didn't know anybody could love
someone as much as you guys love me!

154
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:08,520
What the hell's he doing? What an idiot.

155
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:23,582
Hurry it up, young bassoon,
I need you over here.

156
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,420
Over here, too.

157
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:41,417
Looking nice, you guys.

158
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:42,794
Keep up the good work.

159
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:50,540
Oh, it warms my heart to see those
two working together for once.

160
00:08:50,980 --> 00:08:52,700
I hope you're watching, Tom.

161
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:56,557
It's been a rocky road without you,
but your boys are doing you proud.

162
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:57,637
You might have left us,

163
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:02,661
but watching these two right now is like
seeing the ship you built come alive again.

164
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:12,797
It's finally set.

165
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:15,821
Look, the Log Pose is
pointing to the next island!

166
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:18,257
All that's left is to get our ship.

167
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:19,697
This is gonna be fun!

168
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:21,437
I can't wait to see the ship myself.

169
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:24,077
But Franky said no peeking
until he's finished.

170
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:27,097
By the way, guys, you know
where that log is pointing?

171
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:29,377
Might come as a big surprise
if you're not ready.

172
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:31,225
Actually, I don't have a clue.

173
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:35,800
Come to think of it, it kind of
looks like it's pointing down a bit.

174
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:37,477
You bet it is.

175
00:09:37,560 --> 00:09:40,417
Because where it's pointing
is on the bottom of the ocean.

176
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,520
It's called Fishman Island.

177
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:49,650
What?

178
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,380
We're finally going to
Fishman Island? Really?

179
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:55,700
Whoa, Sanji's acting weird

180
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:58,100
Fishman Island, huh?

181
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:01,160
That's tricky Yeah, I guess so.

182
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:05,047
Is that going to be tough after
what happened in your village?

183
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:07,920
They were pirates.

184
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:10,337
Not all fishmen are going to
give us trouble like that.

185
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:11,250
See?

186
00:10:11,333 --> 00:10:13,077
Everybody knows Fishman Island is awesome.

187
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:14,807
Even Zoro, and he's stupid.

188
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:18,497
Fishman Island is one of the most
famous spots on the whole Grand Line.

189
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:22,237
Beautiful mermaids leap and dive, painting
the water with their elegant tailpits.

190
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:25,237
There you can frolic with the fish
and make all your dreams come true.

191
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:26,940
Help me out, Nino!

192
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:30,330
Ha-ha.

193
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:34,760
Let me dream!

194
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,200
Damn it, I'm not hurting anyone!

195
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:39,900
Relax, there's young mermaids, too.

196
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,277
The thing is, even if the
place is nice to visit,

197
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:45,477
that don't mean it's easy
for people to get there.

198
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:48,617
I assume that was the case, since
it's at the bottom of the sea.

199
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:50,940
Eh, we'll figure it out on the way.

200
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:53,660
Well, on the way is a problem, too.

201
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:57,120
Take a look at today's
paper and you'll understand.

202
00:10:57,920 --> 00:10:59,400
Huh? What is this?

203
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:03,817
Fourteen ships have disappeared this
month alone, all in the same place?

204
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:05,380
I don't understand.

205
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:10,820
They call that patch of water
the Florian Triangle. Anyways,

206
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:15,571
you won't be making it to Fishman Island
until after you sail through there.

207
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:22,300
Every year, over 100 ships go missing in
that area, and nobody has a clue as to why.

208
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:23,860
What's spooky?

209
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:25,057
Is that later?

210
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:29,040
They show up totally empty without
a single crew member in sight.

211
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:32,377
Other people say they found
ghost ships with crews

212
00:11:32,460 --> 00:11:35,980
of dead men wandering
the ocean lost in a haze.

213
00:11:36,140 --> 00:11:38,500
You mean they're like zombies? Scary!

214
00:11:39,340 --> 00:11:41,957
Hanging out with a bunch
of skeletons sounds cool.

215
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:45,620
Hanging out with some
imagination you've got. No way.

216
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:47,120
No ghost ships for us.

217
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:48,157
Not on my watch.

218
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,817
We're passing straight through that place.

219
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:52,076
I mean, what really happens in there?

220
00:11:52,760 --> 00:11:53,697
Who knows?

221
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:59,120
After all, nobody ever comes out of
there alive, and dead men tell no tales.

222
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:01,160
I'd be careful.

223
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:03,780
The water is dark, the fog is thick.

224
00:12:04,020 --> 00:12:05,320
It swallows you up.

225
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:11,880
Many a soul has been sacrificed
to that treacherous sea,

226
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:15,777
so you better be darn ready before
you even think of setting sail.

227
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:18,137
Although some people do
call them ghost ships,

228
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:20,557
abandoned vessels are often
called treasure ships too.

229
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:24,640
We're more likely to find a ship
filled with riches than the undead.

230
00:12:24,820 --> 00:12:25,650
Yeah!

231
00:12:25,733 --> 00:12:26,877
Put time down those ghost ships!

232
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:28,489
All right, leave it to me!

233
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:30,400
No, but I don't want it!

234
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:35,457
I'll stock up on plenty of food and water
before we go, so even if we do get lost,

235
00:12:35,540 --> 00:12:36,370
we'll be fine.

236
00:12:36,453 --> 00:12:37,635
A treasure ship, huh?

237
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:39,397
I wonder if they have swords.

238
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:40,920
Hey, pirate people!

239
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:42,820
Straw Hat!

240
00:12:46,220 --> 00:12:47,400
You need something?

241
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:50,637
Franky wants to talk to you guys.

242
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:52,779
He's got something big to show you.

243
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:56,097
It's been a long night, but they
finished his ship of dreams.

244
00:12:56,180 --> 00:12:58,380
And boy is it super cool!

245
00:12:58,900 --> 00:12:59,730
Yeah!

246
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:01,980
You mean it's done already?

247
00:13:02,180 --> 00:13:04,140
That was really fast! Of course.

248
00:13:04,420 --> 00:13:07,937
That's what happens when the best shipwrights
in the world work around the clock.

249
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:09,077
You better believe it.

250
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:10,097
What are we waiting for?

251
00:13:10,180 --> 00:13:11,320
Let's go! Yeah!

252
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,440
Straw Hats!

253
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:16,440
We got bad news!

254
00:13:17,820 --> 00:13:19,240
Oh, hey, you guys!

255
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:20,720
What's going on?

256
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:21,861
They look upset.

257
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:23,314
I wonder what's wrong.

258
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:30,817
To be honest, we just found
out about this ourselves.

259
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:32,797
Have you seen the wanted posters?

260
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:33,710
Wanted posters?

261
00:13:33,793 --> 00:13:35,717
You've got a huge bounty
on your head, Straw Hat!

262
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:37,976
They're gonna hunt you down for sure!

263
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:40,017
Actually, you've all got bounties!

264
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:41,517
The whole crew is wanted!

265
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:46,280
Took long enough? How much?
Not me too! I want it?

266
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:48,660
No point in talking, just look!

267
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:52,140
Wanted posters for all seven of you.

268
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:59,360
Straw Hat Luffy with a bounty
of 300 million berries.

269
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:02,780
All right, it went up!

270
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:07,120
Pirate Hunter Zoro with a
bounty of 120 million berries.

271
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:13,120
Cat Burglar Nami with a
bounty of 16 million berries.

272
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:19,317
Cotton Candy Lovin' Chopper,
Pet, with a bounty of 50 berries.

273
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,760
50?

274
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:25,680
Demon Child Robin with a
bounty of 80 million berries

275
00:14:30,680 --> 00:14:32,520
Who is that?

276
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:38,440
Black Leg Sanji, attempt to take a
photo, failed Bounty, 77 million berries.

277
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:45,840
Hey, look, Sniper King
has one too, only 15.

278
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:49,677
Well, I know that this is
probably big news for you and all.

279
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:52,457
And I'm sure there's a lot of
pirate stuff you want to talk about.

280
00:14:52,540 --> 00:14:54,097
But, uh, hold on a sec, okay?

281
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:56,857
I came here because I got
a favor to ask of you guys.

282
00:14:56,940 --> 00:14:58,116
Take a look at this.

283
00:14:58,500 --> 00:14:59,330
It's Franky.

284
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:04,280
Cyborg Franky with a bounty
of 44 million berries.

285
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:05,640
This is awful.

286
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:07,757
Big Bro's wanted by the world government.

287
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:09,137
What are we going to do now?

288
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:10,717
Yeah, that's the question.

289
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:13,437
I was happy when I found
out we didn't have bounties.

290
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:15,167
But then this had to happen.

291
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:17,777
Everyone in the whole
city knows about our bro.

292
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:19,697
He can't stay in Water 7 anymore.

293
00:15:19,780 --> 00:15:21,217
And if he gets arrested again,

294
00:15:21,300 --> 00:15:24,097
I don't think we'll have the power
to save him like we did last time.

295
00:15:24,180 --> 00:15:26,415
But I'm sure he worried about us, too.

296
00:15:26,520 --> 00:15:30,977
Knowing him, he probably wouldn't leave the
island no matter how much we begged him.

297
00:15:31,060 --> 00:15:32,237
That's why we came to you.

298
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:34,037
We have no other choice.

299
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:36,197
We're begging you here, Straw Hats!

300
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:37,477
Even if he tries to fight?

301
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:39,577
You gotta take our bro
out to sea with you.

302
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:40,680
Come on!

303
00:15:40,860 --> 00:15:43,389
His parents were pirates
It's in his blood!
